<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head>
<meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ stt.config.title }}</title>
<meta name="description" content="Compare speech-to-text accuracy, model downloads, parameter counts and API rates.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/benchmark.css">
<script>(function(){try{document.documentElement.dataset.theme=localStorage.getItem('bench-theme')||(matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches?'dark':'light')}catch(e){}})();</script>
</head><body><main>
<header class="hero"><div><small class="eyebrow"><a href="/">Voshart / Benchmarks</a> · <a href="/ocr/">OCR</a></small><h1>{{ stt.config.title }}</h1><p>{{ stt.config.description }}</p></div><button class="quiet" id="themeToggle" type="button" aria-label="Toggle light and dark mode">Theme</button></header>
<section class="history-bar" data-release-start="{{ stt.config.release_start }}" data-snapshot-date="{{ stt.config.snapshot_date }}" aria-label="Historical speech model release cutoff">
<div class="hist-head"><span>Model cutoff <strong id="historyDate">{{ stt.config.snapshot_date }}</strong></span><button type="button" class="quiet" id="historyLatest">Latest</button></div>
<input type="range" id="historyRange" min="0" max="365" step="1" value="365" aria-label="Speech model release date cutoff">
<div class="axis"><span id="rangeStart">{{ stt.config.release_start }}</span><span id="rangeEnd">{{ stt.config.snapshot_date }}</span></div><small id="historyStatus">Unknown availability dates appear only in the current view. API rates retain their pricing dates.</small>
</section>
<nav class="views" aria-label="Speech benchmark views">
<button type="button" data-view="matrix" class="active" aria-pressed="true">Matrix</button><button type="button" data-view="english" aria-pressed="false">English</button><button type="button" data-view="longform" aria-pressed="false">Long-form</button><button type="button" data-view="multilingual" aria-pressed="false">Multilingual</button><button type="button" data-view="robustness" aria-pressed="false">Noise & accent</button><button type="button" data-view="small" aria-pressed="false">Small models</button><button type="button" data-view="new" aria-pressed="false">New research</button><button type="button" data-view="secondary" aria-pressed="false">Secondary</button><button type="button" data-view="throughput" aria-pressed="false">Local speed</button><button type="button" data-view="latency" aria-pressed="false">Latency</button><button type="button" data-view="price" aria-pressed="false">Pricing</button>
</nav>
<section id="speechMatrixPanel" aria-label="Speech accuracy matrix">
<div class="controls">
<input id="speechSearch" type="search" placeholder="Search models…" aria-label="Search speech models">
<select id="speechCoverage" aria-label="Primary evidence coverage"><option value="0">All registered</option><option value="1">1+ primary families</option><option value="2" selected>2+ primary families</option><option value="3">3 primary families</option></select>
<select id="speechAccess" aria-label="Speech model access"><option value="all">All models</option><option value="open">Open weights</option><option value="closed">Closed / hosted</option><option value="unknown">Unknown access</option><option value="unreleased">Unreleased weights</option></select>
<select id="speechSort" aria-label="Sort speech models"><option value="score">Highest index / lowest WER</option><option value="download">Smallest download (MB)</option><option value="params">Fewest parameters (M)</option><option value="name">Model name</option><option value="price">Lowest USD / audio hour</option></select>
<select id="speechSize" aria-label="Reported download size"><option value="">All download sizes</option><option value="200">Download ≤200 MB</option><option value="500">Download ≤500 MB</option><option value="1000">Download ≤1,000 MB</option></select>
<select id="speechParams" aria-label="Reported parameter count"><option value="">All parameter counts</option><option value="100">Parameters ≤100 M</option><option value="500">Parameters ≤500 M</option><option value="1000">Parameters ≤1,000 M</option></select>
</div>
<div class="controls" id="speechProtocolControls" hidden>
<select id="speechProtocol" aria-label="Evaluation protocol">{% for id in stt.config.accuracy_tests %}{% for test in stt.accuracyTests %}{% if test.id == id %}<option value="{{ test.id }}"{% if test.id == stt.config.default_test %} selected{% endif %}>{{ test.label }}</option>{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}</select>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="speechMissing"> Include models without a matched result</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="speechExtra"> Additional datasets / languages</label>
</div>
<details class="comparison-note"><summary>About this comparison</summary><p class="key" id="speechProtocolNote">Rank uses distinct English short-form, CORAAL and five-language FLEURS families. WER columns are lower-is-better; the percentile index is higher-is-better. Two mature families permit a provisional index.</p></details>
<p class="key" id="speechStatus" role="status">{{ stt.initial.rows.length }} models · {{ stt.initial.matureCount }} mature core families · default coverage: 2+ primary families</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr id="speechHead">{{ stt.initial | speechMatrixHead | safe }}</tr></thead><tbody id="speechBody">{{ stt.initial | speechMatrixRows(stt) | safe }}</tbody></table></div>
<p class="key">Download is in MB; parameters are in millions (M). Neither is runtime RAM. — means no matched data; size filters exclude unknowns.<br>◊ provisional index (click for details) · † qualified evidence / current service rate.</p>
<noscript><p>The current matrix and source documentation are available without JavaScript. JavaScript enables release replay, detailed protocol views and filters.</p></noscript>
</section>
<section id="speechThroughputPanel" hidden aria-labelledby="throughputTitle">
<h2 id="throughputTitle">Local throughput & load time</h2>
<p class="key">Audio seconds per second of wall time (× realtime), higher is faster. Compare the same workload, hardware, backend and batch size. These are tiny runtime checks, not accuracy families or streaming latency measurements. Model loading is excluded from throughput and shown separately when reported.</p>
<div class="controls"><select id="timingTest" aria-label="Throughput workload">{% for test in stt.throughputTests %}<option value="{{ test.id }}"{% if test.id == 'fermion-20-dictations' %} selected{% endif %}>{{ test.label }}</option>{% endfor %}</select><select id="timingHardware" aria-label="Throughput hardware"><option value="">All hardware</option>{% for hardware in stt.timingHardware %}<option value="{{ hardware }}">{{ hardware }}</option>{% endfor %}</select><select id="timingSample" aria-label="Throughput sample"><option value="">All samples</option><option value="jfk">jfk · 11s</option><option value="dots">dots · 35.332s</option></select><input id="timingSearch" type="search" placeholder="Search runtime models…" aria-label="Search runtime models"></div>
<p class="key" id="timingStatus" role="status">{{ stt.initialTiming.length }} measurements on the selected workload</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="pricing-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Model / configuration</th><th scope="col">× realtime</th><th scope="col">Hardware / runtime</th><th scope="col">Batch</th><th scope="col">Workload / sample</th><th scope="col">Model load</th><th scope="col">Source / run date</th></tr></thead><tbody id="timingBody">{{ stt.initialTiming | speechTiming(stt) | safe }}</tbody></table></div>
</section>
<section id="speechLatencyPanel" hidden aria-labelledby="latencyTitle">
<h2 id="latencyTitle">End-of-utterance response latency</h2>
<p class="key">Moonshine paper Table 2: elapsed time between the end of speech and the returned transcript on an Apple MacBook M3. The source does not identify a p50/p95 statistic or a pinned utterance set. This is separate from time to first token, model loading and throughput. All rows were measured by Moonshine; comparisons to other developers’ models are competitor evidence.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="pricing-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">Response ms ↓</th><th scope="col">Hardware / statistic</th><th scope="col">Operator / source</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for latency in stt.latency %}<tr><th scope="row">{{ stt.modelNames[latency.model] }}</th><td>{{ latency.milliseconds }}</td><td>{{ latency.hardware }}<br><small>Statistic {{ latency.statistic }}</small></td><td class="pricing-note">{{ latency.measurement_operator }} · {{ latency.evidence }} · <a href="{{ stt.sources[latency.source_id].url }}">Paper Table 2 ↗</a></td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
</section>
<section id="speechPricingPanel" hidden aria-labelledby="pricingTitle">
<h2 id="pricingTitle">Published audio tariffs</h2>
<p class="key">Each rate retains provider, currency, tier, mode and date. Minute tariffs are normalized by multiplying by 60. EUR stays EUR. Current service rates do not guarantee the exact model endpoint used in a benchmark. Optional features, volume tiers and promotions affect the bill; see the source configuration.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="pricing-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Model / service</th><th scope="col">Per audio hour</th><th scope="col">Published rate</th><th scope="col">Provider / mode / tier</th><th scope="col">Scope & source</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for price in stt.pricing %}<tr><th scope="row">{{ stt.modelNames[price.model] }}</th><td>{{ price.currency }} {{ price.amount | rate }}</td><td>{{ price.published_amount | rate }} / {% if price.published_unit == 'currency_per_audio_minute' %}min{% else %}hour{% endif %}</td><td>{{ price.provider }} · {{ price.mode }}<br><small>{{ price.tier }} · {{ price.as_of }}</small></td><td class="pricing-note">{{ price.note }} <a href="{{ stt.sources[price.source_id].url }}">Rate card ↗</a></td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
<h2>Audio and text token tariffs</h2>
<p class="key">USD per million tokens. Input audio, input text and output text are different meters. Soniox’s published hourly equivalents depend on a token workload; they are not inserted as flat hourly tariffs. These current service prices do not assign an async benchmark score to a streaming endpoint.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="pricing-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Service</th><th scope="col">Input audio / 1M</th><th scope="col">Input text / 1M</th><th scope="col">Output text / 1M</th><th scope="col">Mode / date / source</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for price in stt.tokenPricing %}<tr><th scope="row">{{ price.provider }} current service</th><td>${{ price.input_audio_usd_per_million_tokens | rate }}</td><td>${{ price.input_text_usd_per_million_tokens | rate }}</td><td>${{ price.output_text_usd_per_million_tokens | rate }}</td><td class="pricing-note">{{ price.mode }} · {{ price.as_of }} · <a href="{{ stt.sources[price.source_id].url }}">Token rate card ↗</a></td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
<p class="key">Self-hosted means deployment-specific compute cost, not zero. No RAM, energy, hosting cost or audio-hour price is inferred from a model download, parameter count, throughput or token rate.</p>
</section>
<details class="method" id="methodology"><summary>Methodology, provenance & sources</summary>
<p>This is an index of published speech recognition evidence. We have not executed the transcription models. WER is 100 × (substitutions + deletions + insertions) / reference words, so it can exceed 100%. Punctuation, diarization, hallucinations and latency need their own measurements.</p>
<p>The core matrix selects three distinct corpus families: the fixed seven-set English short-form panel, CORAAL long-form interviews, and a fixed French/German/Spanish/Italian/Portuguese FLEURS panel. All named components are required for a panel mean. Language CSVs retain separate pinned revisions; no missing language or dataset is filled from another variant. CORAAL alone supplies the long-form core value so Earnings22 is not counted twice. MCV, MLS, extra languages, noise/Monsoon columns and author/runtime variants remain secondary. Hindi Monsoon uses lattice-reference OI-WER with the voi-oiwer scorer; it is not inserted as standard WER or a private Hindi average.</p>
<p>Index is the equal-weight mean of within-family percentile ranks, with midranks for ties. A mature family requires six scored configurations from three organizations. Only one runtime variant for the same weights identity enters a reference cohort, and one selected variant per family contributes. Two mature families permit a provisional index; three remove only the limited-coverage qualification. A lone family is unranked. The default matrix requires two primary families for display; Small models, New research and Secondary expose narrower evidence.</p>
<p>Unknown execution operators, author/competitor/community/imported evidence, conflicting observations, and unknown/unreleased availability qualify an index. Cohort qualifications propagate to every dependent percentile before search or display filters. ◊ exposes actual reasons and every contributing component source on hover or keyboard-accessible click. Publication by a maintainer and source verification do not establish independent reproduction.</p>
<p>The release slider uses verified availability dates, not paper publication, result dates or Hub repository creation. Unknown releases appear only in the current view. Quantized runtime conversions have separate identities and do not inherit upstream release dates, scores, size or memory use. Catalog confidence intervals and sample counts remain in the downloadable data. Legacy-published catalog cells can lack a run date or engine SHA.</p>
<p>Source preference within a matched protocol is maintainer publication, independent third party, community, model author, then vendor/secondary evidence. Alternative observations are preserved; conflicts are not averaged. Assumed, incompatible and private/vendor-internal values cannot supply core coverage, maturity or index. FFASR’s private corpus is not assigned a core vote. The original Phonon-2 164 MB package and its approximately 740 MB GGUF Q8_0 artifact are different configurations.</p>
<p>Further gaps include matched diarization and silence/hallucination tests, broader independently verified release dates, and comparable streaming p50/p95 latency and peak RAM. The latency paper and tiny runtime speed clips do not supply these missing measurements.</p>
<p><a href="/stt/data.json">Download the source data JSON</a> · {{ stt.counts.sources }} documented sources. Prices retain their own as-of dates in historical model views.</p>
<div class="source-grid">{% for id, source in stt.sources %}<p id="source-{{ id }}"><a href="{{ source.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{{ source.title }}</a><br><small>Publication: {{ source.publication_operator }} · execution: {{ source.measurement_operator }} · checked {{ source.verified_on }}. {{ source.note }}</small></p>{% endfor %}</div>
</details>
<footer>Evidence checked {{ stt.config.snapshot_date }} · {{ stt.counts.models }} configurations · <a href="/ocr/">OCR evidence benchmark</a></footer>
</main><script src="/assets/js/ranking.js"></script><script src="/assets/js/rank-ui.js"></script><script src="/assets/js/speech.js"></script><script src="/assets/js/speech-matrix.js"></script><script src="/assets/js/speech-page.js"></script></body></html>
